# What gcloud uploads to Cloud Build for `gcloud run deploy --source .`.
#
# THIS FILE'S EXISTENCE IS THE POINT. Without it, gcloud falls back to
# .gitignore to decide what to upload — and .gitignore excludes data/,
# because the dataset is deliberately not committed. The result is a build
# that succeeds and a service that 500s on every page with
# "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'loader'", since COPY data ./data
# copies a directory containing only .gitkeep.
#
# So: data/ must NOT be excluded here. It is required at runtime — the
# pipeline reads data/inbox and data/attachments, and imports data/loader.py
# by name.
#
# Note a local `docker build` cannot catch this: it uses .dockerignore,
# which has no reason to exclude data/. Only the gcloud upload path does.

# Secrets — never upload.
.env

# Large, platform-specific, rebuilt from requirements.txt inside the image.
.venv/
venv/

.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Not needed to build or run the service.
tests/
docs/
submission.json
